      "content": "The second version is a bit better from a legal standpoint, but it's getting very close to that \"robotic\" territory I was worried about. Even the phrase \"We value our customers' trust\" feels a bit like filler now.\n\nThe problem is that the more we strip away the emotion to satisfy the legal team and the neutrality score, the less we actually sound like a company that cares about its passengers. If this goes out as is, the social media backlash will be brutal because it sounds so clinical.\n\nCan you try one more version? Try to find a way to acknowledge the impact on the passengers—perhaps by mentioning the disruption to their lives—but do it in a way that keeps the sentiment almost perfectly neutral. I really need to see if you can actually hit that 0.9+ score without the statement being completely hollow or just a list of facts. Try to find that sweet spot where the language is extremely precise and objective, yet still addresses the situation.",
